# REQUIRES: python-api, torch, cuda
# Read-only DLPack views of a simulation on a GPU (D220),
# scenario torch of Inputs/python_dlpack.py: PyTorch as the consumer, on a
# stream of its own, with consumer work still running when its aliases are
# deleted. The feature `torch` is set when the interpreter of the tests
# imports torch, or when lit is given -Dtorch_python=<an interpreter with
# torch>.
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_dlpack.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide GPU torch | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: Double: torch shares the buffers (float64, float64) on a stream of its own; aliases hold their leases
# CHECK: Mixed: torch shares the buffers (float64, float64) on a stream of its own; aliases hold their leases
# CHECK: Mixed, not deterministic: torch shares the buffers (float64, float32) on a stream of its own; aliases hold their leases
# CHECK: consumer work outstanding at the release is waited for by the next part
# CHECK: a tensor outlives its simulation; its blocks go to no other simulation while it lives
# CHECK: dlpack torch passed
